[I] scanf for modern C++

[T] scnlib is a modern C++ library replacing scanf for reading and parsing
[T] input, with a std::format-like syntax. It is type-safe, fast and
[T] supports reading from strings, files and standard input, and was
[T] proposed for standardization as std::scan.

[U] https://github.com/eliaskosunen/scnlib

[A] eliaskosunen
[M] andrei32 <andrei32.t2@gmail.com>

[C] extra/tool
[F] CROSS OBJDIR

[L] APL
[V] 4.0.1

[D] b911bec4fc7e017dabbc04b09c104f465dabc7a82789ca5e8a51eb95 scnlib-4.0.1.tar.gz https://github.com/eliaskosunen/scnlib/archive/v4.0.1/

